# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A blank line ends a start tag, and one newline does not"

# A start tag spans lines: TiddlyWiki skips whitespace between attributes, so the attributes of a
# tag broken across lines keep their reading.

<div
#^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.structure.div.start.html.tiddlywiki5
  class="a"
# ^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.structure.div.start.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.attribute.class.html.tiddlywiki5 entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5
  id="b">body</div>
# ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.tag.structure.div.start.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.attribute.id.html.tiddlywiki5 entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5

# A BLANK line ends it. TiddlyWiki reads on — it skips a blank line the same way it skips a
# space, and its own core writes a widget tag across one — but where no pattern matches an end,
# TextMate runs a region to the end of the document, and an unclosed tag then colours every
# construct after it as an attribute name. Counted across 2583 files, no plain HTML start tag
# anywhere carries a blank line, and the six that do all wear a widget name in one core file.

<div

A paragraph, not an attribute.
#^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

<<<
Quoted
#^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.quote.quoteblock.body.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
<<<
